The recorded controllers draw each side's trainer pic from the replay (#20):
RecordedPlayerHandleDrawTrainerPic and RecordedOpponentHandleDrawTrainerPic ask
Replay_GetTrainerPic (src/replay_setup.c), which gives back their own pick unless a replay is
loaded, so every other battle, the expansion's own tests among them, keeps its pic. The near
side's yPos stays the one computed for that pick: every back pic has size 8 (TRAINER_BACK_PIC in
src/data/graphics/trainers.h). The intro ball throw needs no hunk: the throw animates the sprite
the draw made, and BtlController_HandleIntroTrainerBallThrow ignores its palette arguments.

diff --git a/src/battle_controller_recorded_opponent.c b/src/battle_controller_recorded_opponent.c
index 252bc9a8..66962f42 100644
--- a/src/battle_controller_recorded_opponent.c
+++ b/src/battle_controller_recorded_opponent.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "pokeball.h"
 #include "pokemon.h"
 #include "recorded_battle.h"
+#include "replay_interpreter.h"
 #include "reshow_battle_screen.h"
 #include "sound.h"
 #include "string_util.h"
@@ -322,6 +323,7 @@ static void RecordedOpponentHandleDrawTrainerPic(enum BattlerId battler)
         }
     }
 
+    trainerPicId = Replay_GetTrainerPic(battler, trainerPicId);
     BtlController_HandleDrawTrainerPic(battler, trainerPicId, TRUE, xPos, 40, -1);
 }
 
